## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an end-to-end Snowflake ELT for semi-structured logs, including external stages, staging vs. target tables, and simple QC/alerting.

## Key Concepts

- External stages and JSON formats
- Staging vs. target tables
- COPY INTO and data transformation
- TASK scheduling and QC views
- Simple alerting pattern

## Code Example

```sql
CREATE FILE FORMAT jsonfmt TYPE=JSON;
CREATE STAGE s3_logs URL='s3://logs-bucket/app-logs/';
CREATE TABLE LOGS_STG(timestamp_str STRING, user_id STRING, event_type STRING, payload VARIANT);
CREATE TABLE LOGS(timestamp_ntz TIMESTAMP_NTZ, user_id STRING, event_type STRING, payload VARIANT);
COPY INTO LOGS_STG FROM @s3_logs PATTERN='.*app_log.json' FILE_FORMAT=(FORMAT_NAME='jsonfmt');
INSERT INTO LOGS SELECT to_timestamp_ntz(timestamp_str), user_id, event_type, payload FROM LOGS_STG;
CREATE VIEW LOGS_QC AS SELECT date_trunc('DAY', timestamp_ntz) day, COUNT(DISTINCT user_id) users, COUNT(*) events FROM LOGS GROUP BY 1;
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema drift in JSON payloads?
- How would you adjust the pipeline for new fields or partitions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Snowflake-core pipeline design: ingestion, streams, tasks, late data handling, and anomaly scoring across accounts.

## Key Concepts
- Snowflake Streams, Tasks, external stages, MERGE, watermarking, rolling baselines, alerting.
- Data governance: access control, masking, retention.

## Code Example
```sql
-- Core objects (illustrative)
CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE RAW_EVENTS_STAGE URL='s3://region-lake/raw' FILE_FORMAT=(TYPE='JSON');
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE RAW_EVENTS(
  event_id STRING, customer_id STRING, region STRING, amount NUMBER, ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ
);
CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM RAW_EVENTS_STREAM ON TABLE RAW_EVENTS (APPEND_ONLY = FALSE);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_SCORES(customer_id STRING, region STRING, date DATE, score FLOAT);
CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE FRAUD_WATERMARK(date DATE, max_ts TIMESTAMP_NTZ);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test late-arrival handling and boundary conditions?
- How would you scale the rolling baseline computation to thousands of regions and customers?
